// Stone 59 fixture: the refusal walk reads the
// program in its own order, defines where they
// stand. The disk tool stands in the define; the
// guest call stands later, in the main body. The
// disk refusal is the one spoken — the first the
// walk meets.
make sectors() -> number {
    give disksectors()
}

say sectors()
say callguest(2097152, 7)
